dialect grammar
grammar playbook.playbook
extension playbook
use family-scene
start document

# Real grammar for `PlaybookSnapshot::print_dsl`/`parse_dsl`
# (📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs's `print_playbook_snapshot_body`/`parse_playbook_snapshot_body`,
# lines 123-155) — a hand-rolled hex/bracket `key=value` line codec, one line per field, same
# convention `raster.document`/`forms.forms` use. This REPLACES the stale, cross-plugin
# copy-pasted "canvas layer" template (`layers { shape/path/text { canvas-field* } }`,
# `add-layer`/`set-stroke`/`move-layer`/`set-fill`) this file previously carried — see
# `.🧬semio/…/STUBS-AND-PLACEHOLDERS-COMPLETION/📓️grammar-envelope-transcription.md` for how that
# mismatch was discovered (the real committed fixture is a flat hex attribute-list, structurally
# nothing like a layered canvas). Confirmed byte-for-byte against the real committed fixture
# `📚️examples/🎬️demo/🖼️assets/🗣️example.dsl.semio`:
#
#   semio playbook.playbook.dsl v1
#   schema=706c6179626f6f6b2e70726f6772616d
#   id=706c6179626f6f6b
#   version=31
#   title=[0]
#   document=[<hex-child-id>,<hex-target-uri>]
#   flow=[<hex-child-id>,<hex-target-uri>]
artifact-mark = "semio playbook.playbook.dsl v1"
document = artifact-mark schema-line id-line version-line title-line document-line flow-line

schema-line = "schema" "=" hex
id-line = "id" "=" hex
version-line = "version" "=" hex
title-line = "title" "=" opt-hex
document-line = "document" "=" child-handle
flow-line = "flow" "=" child-handle

opt-hex = "[0]" | "[1," hex "]"
child-handle = "[" hex "," hex "]"

# `hex` (bare, deliberately not defined as a local production) is the framework's built-in `hex`
# macro — every hex-bracket-encoded leaf string is `enc_str` (lowercase-hex UTF-8 bytes).
